r-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317656/field-3/b636d825ad8866ce3c8a91e491f41cfbf770a963a59c661f3f5b0fe6612b0cc3" :answer-field/choices ["q-317656/field-3/b636d825ad8866ce3c8a91e491f41cfbf770a963a59c661f3f5b0fe6612b0cc3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317656" :question/id #uuid "045d61b4-60dc-5b8e-a5ef-7c171a479374" :question/math-academy-id "q-317656" :question/problem "Let $r=⟨2,-1,3⟩$ and $s=⟨5,1,-4⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $s$ onto $r.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{r}\\,s=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{r}\\,s & =\\frac{r\\cdot s}{r\\cdot r}r \\\\  & =\\frac{{r}_{x}{s}_{x}+{r}_{y}{s}_{y}+{r}_{z}{s}_{z}}{{r}_{x}^{2}+{r}_{y}^{2}+{r}_{z}^{2}}r \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 5+(-1)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-4)}{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}}r \\\\  & =\\frac{10-1-12}{4+1+9}⟨2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{14}⟨2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,-\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{3}{14},-\\frac{9}{14}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317656/field-1" "q-317656/field-2" "q-317656/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317656"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
